  "notes": "Bullet 3 -- 'After trading the items, your Gobbiebag capacity will be increased' -- is an OUTCOME, not an action. A keyword parser would emit it as a step and leave the marker pointing at a thing you cannot do. Two steps, both on Bluffnix, so the marker never moves; the gain here is a working turn-in, which this quest never had. This is also the quest that forced `alt` to mean an ALTERNATIVE rather than an extra condition: a single Goblin Stew REPLACES all four items, so conjoining them would be wrong in precisely the case the field was added for. Verified both routes reach yellow. VERIFY: the alternative was recorded as the item \"Goblin Stew\", but the page -- Item Reqs and bullet 2 -- names only \"Goblin Stew 880\", which is a DIFFERENT item: res/items.lua 4094 (Goblin Stew 880) vs 4465 (Goblin Stew, an unrelated usable food). As recorded, carrying any Goblin Stew would have turned the trade step yellow. This pass may not rename an item, so the alt is dropped and items_partial records that a real alternative exists which the verifier may not name. The four-item primary path is exactly what the page says and is untouched. \"or_branch_modelled\" is now stale -- see \"or_branch_unmodelled\". The claim in this note that both routes were verified to reach yellow cannot distinguish the two stews, so it does not vouch for the name.\n\nMoved out of the player-facing step notes (build vocabulary; see AUTHORING.md, 'Two notes, two audiences'):\n  step 2: so the AND-list records it.",
