  "notes": "The best case in the corpus for step tracking: nine key items granted in order, all of which resolve exactly against res/key_items.lua. Bullet 4 is ONE wiki bullet holding three independent journeys to three different cities, so it is split into three steps -- source_bullets records that. The infobox says the giver is Nashmeira in the Imperial Ward, but the walkthrough opens on Naja Salaheem in Whitegate (I-10); the walkthrough is what you actually do, so step 1 follows it. VERIFY: bullet 4 says the three nation visits \"can be done in any order\", but steps 4-6 carry group=null, so the ladder forces San d'Oria -> Bastok -> Windurst and will point at Halver even for a player who went to Kupipi first -- the exact failure AUTHORING describes under Groups. A group may not be added by this pass, so the three steps and the quest are demoted and unordered_group is flagged instead. Step 11's \"blank target\" is the page describing an UNNAMED clickable on the dark lamp, not an entity name; it resolves to no marker key, so the name is dropped and the description stays in the note. Also flagged: the header giver (Nashmeira, Imperial Ward) disagrees with the walkthrough's Naja Salaheem, which the note already described but nothing flagged; and Quest Reqs \"Eternal Mercenary (Complete all ToAU Missions)\" is a mission gate that nothing in gates models. Names all resolve, including the nine key items and Plumbago (2860, same id as the page's \"Slab of Plumbago\").",
